.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt SLENDMAIL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm slendmail ,
.Nm sendmail ,
.Nm newaliases ,
.Nm mailq
.Nd deliver the mail of system tools to chat and webhook services
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl tiIv
.Op Fl f Ar sender
.Op Fl F Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar option
.Op Fl b Ar mode
.Op Fl q Ns Op Ar interval
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar recipient ...
.Nm
.Fl -version | -help
.Nm newaliases
.Nm mailq
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads one message on standard input and delivers it to the targets of
.Pa /etc/slendmail.conf .
It is installed as
.Pa /usr/sbin/sendmail
and accepts the command lines of cron, at, sudo, mdadm, mailx and similar
callers.
.Pp
Flags follow
.Xr getopt 3 :
a value is glued
.Pq Fl froot
or the next argument
.Pq Fl f Ar root ,
flags without a value group
.Pq Fl ti ,
and
.Fl -
ends the options.
Options and recipients may come in any order before
.Fl - .
The value of a flag is never read as an option.
An unknown flag is logged and ignored.
.Pp
Recipients are the arguments, split at commas, and with
.Fl t
the addresses of the To, Cc and Bcc headers, without duplicates.
A message with a Resent-To, Resent-Cc or Resent-Bcc header, even an empty one,
is a resent message: then
.Fl t
takes the addresses of these three headers instead.
Bcc and Resent-Bcc headers are removed from the message.
.Pa /etc/aliases
and
.Pa .forward
are not read.
.Pp
The text of a notification is the text/plain part of the message, else its
text/html part converted to text; other parts are attachments.
The conversion collapses white space outside pre elements and reduces several
empty lines in a row to one everywhere, pre elements included.
Encoded words, quoted-printable and base64 are decoded and every charset is
converted to UTF-8.
A body declared US-ASCII, or in an unknown charset, that is valid UTF-8 is
taken as UTF-8.
Text without a charset or declared US-ASCII that is not valid UTF-8, and text
declared ISO-8859-1, is read as windows-1252.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar sender , Fl r Ar sender
Envelope sender, angle brackets around it removed; an empty value or
.Li <>
is the null sender.
Without a value or with a line break the call exits 64.
.It Fl F Ar name
Full name of the sender; a line break exits 64.
.It Fl t
Take recipients from the To, Cc and Bcc headers as well, or only from the
Resent-To, Resent-Cc and Resent-Bcc headers when the message has any of them.
.It Fl i , Fl oi
A line with a single dot is ordinary text.
Without it such a line ends the message, and the first dot of a line
starting with two dots is removed.
.It Fl o Ar option
Ignored, except
.Fl oi .
.It Fl b Ar mode
The first letter decides:
.Cm m
delivers, the default;
.Cm i
does nothing;
.Cm p
lists the queue;
.Cm s
is refused with exit status 64; other modes are ignored with a warning.
.It Fl q Ns Op Ar interval
Runs the queue once; the interval is ignored.
.It Fl I
Does nothing, like
.Fl bi .
.It Fl C Ar file
Ignored with a warning.
.It Fl B , Fl h , Fl L , Fl N , Fl O , Fl R , Fl V , Fl X , Fl p , Fl A
Take a value and are ignored.
.It Fl d , Fl e
Ignored; the value is glued or the next argument unless it starts with a
dash.
.It Fl v , Fl m , Fl n , Fl U , Fl G
Ignored.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Read another configuration file; ignored with a warning when the setgid
bit of the binary applies to a caller other than root.
.It Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl -help
Print a usage summary.
.El
.Pp
Called as
.Nm newaliases
the program does nothing; called as
.Nm mailq
it lists the queue.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SLENDMAIL_CONFIG
Another configuration file, like
.Fl -config .
.It Ev EMAIL , Ev USER , Ev LOGNAME
Sender of a message without
.Fl f
and without a From header; ignored when the setgid bit applies.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/slendmail.conf
The configuration.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
At least one target accepted the message, or a mode without a message
succeeded.
.It 64
Usage error: a sender flag without a value, a line break in an address
or in the full name,
.Fl bs ,
or a mode that does not exist yet.
.It 66
Standard input cannot be read.
.It 69
No target accepted the message.
.It 70
Internal error.
.It 77
A service mode requested by a caller without the right to it.
.It 78
The configuration cannot be read or is invalid.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr cron 8
